<!--
  The themed-icon layer (Android 13+): the same notebook as ic_launcher_foreground, reduced to one
  silhouette.

  WHY THIS IS NOT JUST THE FOREGROUND. The system reads only the alpha of whatever <monochrome>
  points at and fills it with a wallpaper-derived colour, so pointing it at the colour artwork
  unions the sheets, the ribbon and the shading into a single featureless blob — the drawing
  survives only as an outline. Every separation there is carried by colour, and colour is exactly
  what the themed pass throws away. So the detail has to be cut into the shape itself, as holes.

  HOW IT IS BUILT. Generated from assets/icon_mk3.svg by boolean geometry, not by hand:

    middle' = middle - (cover translated down 16)
    bottom' = bottom - (middle translated down 16)
    result  = (cover u middle' u bottom') - (ribbon dilated by 6)

  The two subtractions open a gap where each sheet passes under the one above it, so the stack
  reads as three layers rather than one lump. Translating the upper shape down is what carves that
  gap, and it works because these sheets are stacked vertically — it is not a general offset.
  Subtracting the ribbon last turns it from a black stripe into a slit, which is the one feature
  that says notebook rather than paper.

  The cover and bottom shapes taken here are mk3's #3F3839 underlays, not the sheets they sit
  behind: the underlay is the outer two units of each dark layer, so it is what defines the
  silhouette's edge. Taking the sheet instead loses two units all round, invisibly at full size.
  mk3's 12 per cent shading wash is ignored — it covers most of the stack, and any alpha it
  contributes would fill the gaps back in.

  STILL MK3'S, AFTER THE FOREGROUND MOVED TO MK5, and deliberately. What mk5 changed is colour: the
  bottom sheet's #3F3839 hairline became a #907878 border so it would show against the dark tile,
  and this layer discards colour by definition — the same geometry, lit differently, is the same
  silhouette. Checked rather than assumed: mk5's bottom underlay is byte-identical to mk3's, and the
  two silhouettes rendered at launcher scale differ in 285 pixels of 104,976, a hairline along the
  fore edge where mk5 adds a small wedge. Below anything the themed pass can show. If mk5's outline
  is ever genuinely edited, this has to be rebuilt from it — the boolean recipe above is the whole
  of the method, and the numbers below it are judged at 48px.

  THE TWO NUMBERS. 16 source units is 1.5dp at this scale, and 6 is the radius the ribbon is
  widened by before it is cut out. Both were chosen by rendering at 48px, not by eye at full size:
  gaps of 10 close up at launcher scale and the stack goes back to a lump, 22 eats into the sheets;
  an undilated ribbon is the artwork's own width, which survives at 105px and vanishes at 48. Judge
  any change to them at 48px.

  SIZE AND CENTRING are the foreground's, unchanged and deliberately so — same 62dp width, same
  offsets, same 0.094946 scale — so the themed icon sits exactly where the colour one does. See the
  long note in ic_launcher_foreground.xml before touching them.

  The fill colour below is arbitrary and is discarded; only the alpha is read. Do not hand-edit the
  path — re-run the boolean build against the source instead.
-->
